+<dialog id="privacy-dialog"><button class="dialog-close" aria-label="Close dialog">×</button><div class="eyebrow">A LITTLE TRANSPARENCY</div><h2>Private notes, explained.</h2><p>This homepage is a local encryption demo. A temporary recipient key pair is created in your browser. Your note is encrypted and held in memory; it is never sent to the shop or stored on disk. Reloading the page removes your note and keys.</p><p>Classical uses X25519 key agreement. Hybrid combines X25519 and ML-KEM-768. Post-quantum uses ML-KEM-768 encapsulation. Each mode derives an AES-256-GCM key using HKDF-SHA-256, with a fresh salt and nonce. The delivery label is encrypted along with your note.</p><p>A real delivery service needs an authenticated recipient public key and a secure backend for authorized staff to decrypt notes. This demo does not authenticate a delivery recipient.</p><a href="https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">About the cryptography library ↗</a></dialog>
+<dialog id="note-dialog"><button class="dialog-close" aria-label="Close dialog">×</button><div class="eyebrow">DECRYPTED IN YOUR BROWSER</div><h2 id="saved-label">Your delivery note</h2><p id="decrypted-note"></p><p class="dialog-muted">This preview uses the temporary recipient key from this page session.</p><button id="download" class="primary-button">Download encrypted note <span>↓</span></button></dialog>
+</body></html>
